# A name field whose bytes after the terminator are not zero. The medium
# can carry one — whatever wrote it need not have been this library — and
# the ports have to agree on whether it matches, so the comparison must
# stop at the terminator instead of sweeping the whole field.
#
# The first file header sits at 256: name "a" at 256, terminator at 257,
# padding from 258. Dirty the padding and reseal, so the header is legally
# WRITTEN rather than corrupt and the readers get past the CRC gate.
init zeros 8192
format 4
add a fill:1:16
add bb fill:2:16
poke 258 7a
poke 259 7a
poke 260 ff
reseal 256
# Every reader must still see the file as "a": enumeration, the in-memory
# read, and the bounded-RAM walker alike.
list
read a 8192
walk a
# The chain past it is untouched, so the second file is still reachable.
walk bb
# A target that equals the dirty bytes must NOT match — the padding is
# not part of the name.
walk azz
